  "release_notes": [
    "Release 0.1.6 of the Gov OS, built from b8a04194a3370ce4e629563921f49e25533cd290 on w2/integrate.",
    "- Merge e2/fix-phase0-reds: the 0.1.6 release suite's Phase 0 reds fixed in the tests (W2-116 S2 states P0-1's due rule; W2-208 P0-3 no longer depends on the time of day)",
    "- Merge e2/fix-walls: the 0.1.6 release suite's wall reds fixed in the tests (FM-5's Stop block, the writer's only, stated as the one allowed difference; every other byte still compared)",
    "- The two Phase 0 acceptance reds are wrong tests: S2's second-time case states P0-1's due rule; the W2-208 only-committed case plants the clock",
    "- Tests: the wall comparisons state the Stop hook as the one allowed difference (FM-5, DEC-1248)",
    "- The tracked start_lead.sh starts leads at effort medium, as the rubric's lead row says (DEC-1236 (2); T-10: the start scripts match the table exactly); found by the models-by-role lead",
    "- I-29 logged: the 0.1.6 release suite's 10 reds the landings' selections missed (walls after FM-5; Phase 0's due rule and kit hook)",
    "- Two fix leads' briefs for the 0.1.6 release suite's ten reds (the walls after FM-5; Phase 0's due rule and kit hook)",
    "- Version 0.1.6 for patch release 0.1.6 (DEC-1248): EXAMIN's measure fixed at the root (each writer's questions form-checked by code before its session ends, refused ones returned to it, proven in a real writer session; round 2 gets the pre-flight refusals; the void said at once; every stop names its cause), the I-17 wheel fix, Phase 0's memory first (the refresh retried and checked, the kit installs the git hook), the kit's licence file",
    "- Merge e2/fix-memaudit-3: FM-1 proven in the real writer launch (FM-5): the writer's launch line, the wall's Stop hook and its write permissions; a real writer session refused a planted form fault and repaired it before its session ended",
    "- FM-5: the writer's permission rules use the double slash of an absolute path",
    "- FM-5: the writer's settings grant Write/Edit into out/, the launch asks no permission prompts",
    "- W2-204 FM-5: the writer's settings grant Write/Edit into out/ and the launch asks no permission prompts",
    "- W2-204 S9: the writer brief prints the BRIEF line plus one LAUNCH writer line (FM-5)",
    "- FM-5: the writer launch line, the wall's Stop hook, writer-run",
    "- DEC-1249 (2) interim: Gov OS's project settings deny reads and edits of both hidden sets roots, and shell commands naming EXAMIN's (I-28), until the eval-roots fix lands",
    "- W2-204 FM-5 acceptance tests: the launch line, the wall's Stop hook, writer-run (red on the base)",
    "- FM-5: the K-line (the check runs in every real writer launch)",
    "- The fix-memaudit-3 lead's brief (FM-5: the writer check proven in the real writer launch; gates 0.1.6), its memory bundle pasted uncut",
    "- Merge e2/fix-memaudit: the fresh 80's writer loop (FM-1 to FM-4): writer-check and deliver run pre-flight's own per-question checks and refuse with codes only; round 2 gets the pre-flight-1 refusals; the void said at once; every stop names its cause",
    "- The eval-roots lead's brief (DEC-1249 (2), I-28: ER-1 to ER-5), with its memory bundle pasted uncut (DEC-1249 (1))",
    "- DEC-1249: memory first by construction per role (bundle profiles, never cut a result, every return lists its retrieves); every hidden sets root refused by code to non-measure sessions; I-28 logged; LEAD-COMMON carries the rules",
    "- W2-204 README map: FM-1..FM-4 and P0-2 keyed success-20..24 so gov accept reads them",
    "- The fresh 80's writer loop: writer-check Stop hook, deliver pre-flight, round-2 refusals, void at once, causes (FM-1 to FM-4)",
    "- Acceptance tests for the fresh 80's writer loop fix (FM-1 to FM-4)",
    "- Merge w2/integrate into e2/fix-memaudit; DAEO-ma4q: KPI lines FM-1 to FM-4 per the owner's order (Stop hook, round-2 refusals, void at once, causes)",
    "- Merge e2/phase0-memory: Phase 0, memory first (plan items 0-1 to 0-3): the refresh retried and checked, the store behind HEAD named by status, retrieve and brief; memaudit preflight refuses STORE_BEHIND; the kit carries and installs the git hook",
    "- Merge branch 'w2/integrate' into e2/fix-memaudit",
