    "- Briefs for the 0.1.6 streams (Phase 0; the W2-207 machine-wide gate with MA-6 and MG-1 to MG-5; models and effort by role through the kit; W2-211 decisions-by-page slice (a) with the escalation rubric's first slice; the I-17 fix); I-18 and I-19 logged from EXAMIN",
    "- Plan item 0-4: all rights reserved, stated in LICENSE at the root and in the kit (DEC-1244 Q-11 (b)); I-17 logged (gov update rebuilds a wheel whose hash differs from the cut one; EXAMIN's EF-4)",
    "- The practice-first decisions page, read and published (DEC-1245 (4)): counts and release facts brought up to the 0.1.5 cut",
    "- DEC-1247: W2-207's gate keeps 2 GB free below WSL's cap and reads Windows' free memory, holding new work when it runs low (MA-6)",
    "- Handover: the EXAMIN CTO's handover path (docs/audits/wave0/FRESH-START-2026-11-24.md, 2ae6747)",
    "- Handover: re-run the post-landing check the restart cuts off",
    "- The CTO's handover of 2026-11-24 before the WSL restart: 0.1.5 cut and pinned, the authority file on, the plans, the next release 0.1.6, the next actions in order (start the EXAMIN and ASMO OS CTOs fresh)",
    "- The authority file on: the CTO cuts releases whose content the owner approved, by code, once the release acceptance passes, with the re-pin's self-rollback and a push each time (DEC-1223 RB-1, DEC-1226, DEC-1235 (2)); turned on after the owner's cut of 0.1.5, his last manual cut",
    "- DEC-1246 (ASMO OS one product with UPIM inside, its CTO at the restart; the machine-wide gate, models by role in code and usage per repository in the next release); the ASMO OS CTO's start brief; the practice-first proposals and their decisions page (drafted, to be read and published by the fresh session)",
    "- Re-pin from release 0.1.5: gov from the release's wheel (tag v0.1.5, commit ba09214f2024)",
